# tools/g/generated_page_freshness_witness.rish -- the commit that moves a generated page's numbers refreshes it.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. Two pages here are GENERATED and compared against a fresh render by a standing
# guard: README.md's four front-door numbers and the crushed library index at
# docs-geode/libraries/README.md. Both count witnesses and Rye modules, which is what most laps here
# add. So a page goes stale inside the very commit that made it stale, and the drift shows up on the
# next cold start rather than on the lap that earned it. Three times in two days: the roster's first
# honest run found the front door reading fascia 45 when the tree read 41 (REDS %151), the next cold
# start found 1,650 witnesses when the tree held 1,651 (REDS %152), and the run after that caught
# the library index the same way -- on the very lap that added this witness.
#
# The discipline was already written -- "Add a witness or a module and this block goes stale, so it
# is regenerated in the same commit", at the head of tools/fixtures/readme_metrics_scan.sh. A rule
# living in a comment is a rule no program runs, which is exactly what REDS %150 paid to learn about
# the standing-equipment roster. tools/hooks/pre-commit is that comment made executable.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal, on a throwaway repository:
#   A docs-only commit invokes no generator -- a ten-second render on every commit is a hook the
#     bench would learn to route around, so resting is a proven behavior rather than a hope.
#   A witness added with both pages clean refreshes BOTH and stages them into that same commit.
#   A witness added while a page carries the author's own unstaged edits is REFUSED, with the
#     refreshed page left in the worktree and nothing of the author's swept into the commit.
#   Once the page is staged as the refusal asked, the commit proceeds and adds nothing further.
#   A tree with no rishi on disk commits exactly as before -- the depersonalized seed's case.
# And in the field: this clone's core.hooksPath names the tree's own tracked hooks, and the
#   pre-commit file is executable, since git skips a non-executable hook in silence.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That the fascia grade and the rooms-over-bound count are current -- both can
# drift from a commit adding no witness and no module, and this rung is silent about both. The
# rostered readme_metrics guard still catches them at a cold start. This closes the fast, frequent
# half of the drift, and says so rather than implying it closed the whole.
#
# Kin: tools/hooks/pre-commit (the wall), tools/fixtures/generated_page_freshness_control.sh (the five
# cases), tools/r/readme_metrics.rish (the generator), tools/r/readme_metrics_witness.rish (the block's
# own freshness guard), tools/i/install_hooks.rish (the arming).
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/g/generated_page_freshness_witness.rish

say "generated-page-freshness: Language EN -- a generated number is worth more than a typed one only while it is regenerated, so the commit that moves it is the commit that refreshes it."
say "generated-page-freshness: Style Radiant -- five behaviors proven on a throwaway repository over both generated pages, and the honest silence about fascia named rather than implied."
say "generated-page-freshness: Lens TAME -- safety first: the hook stages only its own regeneration, and refuses rather than sweep an author's unstaged edits into a commit they never wrote."

let hook = "tools/hooks/pre-commit"

let present = run ["sh" "-c" "test -f ${hook}"]
assert present.ok else "generated-page-freshness: ${hook} is missing -- the wall is not in the tree"

let runnable = run ["sh" "-c" "test -x ${hook}"]
assert runnable.ok else "generated-page-freshness: ${hook} is not executable -- git would skip it in silence"

let armed = run ["git" "config" "--get" "core.hooksPath"]
assert armed.ok else "generated-page-freshness: core.hooksPath is unset -- run rishi/bin/rishi run tools/i/install_hooks.rish"
assert (trim armed.out) == "tools/hooks" else "generated-page-freshness: core.hooksPath reads ${armed.out} rather than tools/hooks"
say "field GREEN -- the hook stands in the tree, executable, and this clone is armed to run it"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/generated_page_freshness_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "generated-page-freshness: the control must complete -- see stderr"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "docs_free=yes" else "generated-page-freshness: a docs-only commit must invoke no generator"
assert control.out contains "clean_staged=yes" else "generated-page-freshness: a witness added with the pages clean must refresh and stage both in that commit"
assert control.out contains "dirty_refused=yes" else "generated-page-freshness: a stale page beside unstaged edits must refuse rather than sweep them in"
assert control.out contains "fresh_quiet=yes" else "generated-page-freshness: once the page is staged the commit must proceed and add nothing further"
assert control.out contains "no_rishi_free=yes" else "generated-page-freshness: a tree without rishi must commit exactly as before"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "generated-page-freshness: the control must agree with itself"
say "RED and GREEN paths proven -- one refusal, three welcomes, and one rest"

say "GREEN: generated-page-freshness -- the commit that moves a generated page's numbers is the commit that refreshes it."
